# .worktreeinclude
#
# Files listed here are propagated from the main repo into a newly-created
# git worktree by `scripts/worktree-setup.sh`. Use this for untracked dev-
# only files (env vars, local overrides) that don't live in git but are
# needed for the worktree to be runnable.
#
# Mechanism: each path becomes a symlink in the worktree pointing back at
# the file in the main repo. Symlink, not copy — so editing a dev env var
# in the main repo propagates to every active worktree without re-running
# setup.
#
# Format:
#   - One path per line, relative to repo root.
#   - Lines starting with `#` are comments.
#   - Blank lines ignored.
#
# Notes on what NOT to include:
#   - `node_modules/` — pnpm install per worktree; pnpm's content-addressable
#     store at ~/.pnpm-store/ makes reinstall fast and disk-efficient.
#   - `dist/` — each worktree builds its own.
#   - `.dolt/` — beads handles worktree access via its `redirect` mechanism
#     (`bd worktree create` sets this up automatically); never symlink the
#     dolt DB directly (concurrent-access hazard).
#   - `tmp/`, `.terraform/`, `*.tfstate` — ephemeral or sensitive; keep
#     scoped to the workspace that produced them.

backend/.env.development
